  </diagram>

  <diagram id="page-why" name="3. Why Azure's filter does not apply">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1300" pageHeight="940" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="w_title" value="Why Azure's content filter does not apply to Claude - the documented chain" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="16" width="1220" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w_sub" value="This is not a quirk of one deployment. It follows from how Microsoft scopes the guardrail system, in three documented hops." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="48" width="1220" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;b&gt;1. The guardrail system is scoped to models sold by Azure&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;&quot;The guardrail system applies to all Foundry Models sold by Azure, except for prompts and completions processed by audio transcription models.&quot;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px&quot;&gt;learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/guardrails/guardrails-overview&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="90" width="600" height="106" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;b&gt;2. Claude is not in that category&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;&quot;You access Claude models in Microsoft Foundry through Foundry Models from partners and community. Models ... that Anthropic sells and operates are Non-Microsoft Products.&quot;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;True for &lt;b&gt;both&lt;/b&gt; hosting options: &quot;Hosted on Azure&quot; changes where inference runs, not who sells and operates the model.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px&quot;&gt;.../concepts/claude-models and .../concepts/claude-models-hosting-comparison&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="236" width="600" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;b&gt;3. Microsoft names a different safety layer for Claude&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hosting comparison lists &lt;b&gt;Content safety: &quot;Anthropic safety systems active&quot;&lt;/b&gt; for both options - not Azure content filters.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;&quot;Claude models in Microsoft Foundry use Anthropic safety systems and safeguards ... To learn more about harmful content screening ... see Anthropic's documentation.&quot;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px&quot;&gt;.../responsible-ai/claude-models/data-privacy&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="416" width="600" height="146" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="concl" value="&lt;b&gt;=&amp;gt; There is no Azure-configurable content control on the Anthropic surface&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px&quot;&gt;Screening still happens - it is Anthropic's, and it is the model vendor's, not a control surface Azure hands you.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="260" y="602" width="680" height="76" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="trap" value="&lt;b&gt;The trap: raiPolicyName is still accepted&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px&quot;&gt;It lives on Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts/deployments, an ARM type shared by every deployment flavour, so ARM stores and echoes it for any deployment. Our &quot;claude-strict&quot; policy - all four categories blocking at Low - shows as attached in the portal and in az, and enforces nothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;A control that is configured, reported and inert is worse than an absent one, because it passes review.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="260" y="708" width="680" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="fix" value="&lt;b&gt;The fix: enforce outside the deployment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px&quot;&gt;APIM + Content Safety (this repo, client-agnostic) - or call Content Safety from your own app, if you own every caller.&lt;br&gt;Both call the same classifiers; only the placement differs.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="260" y="858" width="680" height="76" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="side" value="&lt;b&gt;&quot;Foundry Models sold by Azure&quot;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px&quot;&gt;the catalogue the guardrail system covers&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px&quot;&gt;Azure OpenAI&lt;br&gt;Microsoft&lt;br&gt;Black Forest Labs&lt;br&gt;Moonshot AI&lt;br&gt;xAI&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Anthropic does not appear.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px&quot;&gt;Point-in-time, verified on this deployment. Re-run Test-Guardrails.ps1 after Foundry updates - the Bicep already declares the strict posture, so if Microsoft extends enforcement you get it for free and the test starts reporting BLOCKED-PLATFORM.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="90" width="300" height="472" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="w1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" target="s2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" target="s3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="concl">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="concl" target="trap">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="trap" target="fix">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
